{#-
  The KOF XI corner disc (top-right of the main menu), rebuilt 1:1
  from the reference frame. R = 100 units = the grey plate:
    · white halo ring to 1.38R carries the ring text; BOTH clip at
      the screen frame's inner edge (they slide under the border —
      only the hard disc overlaps the border)
    · the hard disc is a light grey plate to 1.0R with an orange
      outline ring at 1.02R; the dark rings at 0.766R (thick) and
      0.625R (thin) and the green core sit ON the plate, and the
      "segment gaps" are plate-grey cross lines that spin in sync
      with the background disc's spokes (48s), painted over the rings
    · green ring 0.36–0.51R with dark olive edges, warm cream center
    · green ball at 50.6° / 1.205R in a plate-grey housing, joined to
      the plate by a flared grey bridge (over the orange outline) —
      one continuous grey piece, like the original
    · ring text on a 1.07R circle, rotating, big chunky caps
  viewBox starts at 0 0 (not centered) so the rotors' CSS
  transform-origin 50% 50% resolves unambiguously to the center;
  static geometry is translated to (145,145).

  Three stacked divs share the same geometry, painted in DOM order:
  clipped halo + ring text, then the hard disc, then the bridge +
  ball (which the text slides under in turn).
-#}
<div class="cdisc cdisc--halo" aria-hidden="true">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 290 290" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
    <defs>
      {#- near-full circle; the endpoint must sit just BEFORE the start
          along the clockwise travel (i.e. slightly below it) so the arc
          resolves to the (145,145)-centered circle, not the mirror one -#}
      <path id="cd-text-ring" d="M 38 145 A 107 107 0 1 1 38 145.01" fill="none"/>
    </defs>
    <g transform="translate(145 145)">
      <circle r="138" class="cd-halo"/>
    </g>
    <g class="cd-rotor">
      <text class="cd-text"><textPath href="#cd-text-ring" textLength="655" lengthAdjust="spacing">{{ (site.name + " " + site.name) | upper }}</textPath></text>
    </g>
  </svg>
</div>

<div class="cdisc" aria-hidden="true">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 290 290" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
    <g transform="translate(145 145)">
      <circle r="102" class="cd-outline"/>
      <circle r="100" class="cd-plate"/>
      <circle r="76.6" class="cd-ring cd-ring--thick"/>
      <circle r="62.5" class="cd-ring cd-ring--thin"/>
    </g>

    <g class="cd-cross-rotor">
      <g class="cd-cross" transform="translate(145 145) rotate(7)">
        <line x1="-86" y1="0" x2="86" y2="0"/>
        <line x1="0" y1="-86" x2="0" y2="86"/>
      </g>
    </g>

    <g transform="translate(145 145)">
      <circle r="54.3" class="cd-edge"/>
      <circle r="51.2" class="cd-green"/>
      <circle r="36.2" class="cd-edge"/>
      <circle r="31.1" class="cd-center"/>
    </g>
  </svg>
</div>

<div class="cdisc cdisc--ball" aria-hidden="true">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 290 290" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
    {#- flared bridge from the plate to the ball housing, along the
        ball's radial; both ends hide under same-grey shapes so the
        whole thing reads as one piece -#}
    <g transform="translate(145 145) rotate(50.6)">
      <path class="cd-bridge" d="M 88 -16 Q 102 -11 112 -10 L 112 10 Q 102 11 88 16 Z"/>
    </g>
    <g transform="translate(145 145)">
      <circle cx="76.5" cy="93.1" r="17.5" class="cd-plate"/>
      <circle cx="76.5" cy="93.1" r="12.6" class="cd-edge"/>
      <circle cx="76.5" cy="93.1" r="11.1" class="cd-ball"/>
    </g>
  </svg>
</div>
